L000418	The periodograms of the calcium indicators from all three analyzed epochs reveal what we interpret as the primary SPI signals (H-08: 2.81\,d, C-16: 2.81\,d, C-24: 2.46\,d) and their potential $\pm$~1-day aliases. In H-08, the alias is slightly stronger than the primary signal, while in C-16 and C-24, the primary signal dominates. To validate our interpretation of the primary signals and aliases, we use the code \texttt{AliasFinder} \cite{Stock_2020}.
L000419	This method is based on the work from \cite{DawsonFabrycky2010ApJ...722..937D} and has been used in \cite{Trifon_2018} to determine the true signals in radial velocity attributed to the planetary companion GJ~436~b (2.64\,d vs. its 1-day alias at 1.6\,d). The relatively weak power of the peaks in all the three epochs analyzed did not yield any significant results using \texttt{AliasFinder} (Figs.~\ref{fig:AliasFinder_H08},\ref{fig:AliasFinder_C16},\ref{fig:AliasFinder_C24}).
